s  so much of what makes this Arc  interesting and possible and from the  very beginning he's deceitful but we let  it go due to how the ark manages our  attention and as the beat plot develops  we become more and more in need of  allies for Ichigo to latch onto as the  world comes crumbling down around him  thanks to tsukushima's mind manipulation  ability and once the perfect moment  reveals herself for ginjo to get his  mask off moment it is there for us to  relish it it's perfectly placed whether  or not I saw it coming is sort of  irrelevant I had my suspicions but  wasn't convinced but what I appreciated  was how it makes sense and how perfectly  timed the execution of this reveal was  the arc itself is wonderfully focused  and knows exactly what it wants to be  delivering this interesting contrast not  only between Ichigo and ginjou but  Ichigo and his former self I didn't  mention this at the beginning of the  video but the beginning of this Arc  shows a very clear contrast address  between the present now in this Arc and  the very first chapter of this series  but what's more is that I noticed in  this Arc more than any other I've read  it comes across as a contrast and  callback to the first Arc as a whole and  highlights how each and every Central  character has grown each go a character  that was once learning how to adopt  responsibility now yearnsford is  searching for it he wants to protect his  friends oruhime and Chad who are  characters that were left out in the  cold left entirely in the dark for so  much of that first Arc are instead the  ones now leaving Ichigo in the dark  trying to save him from trouble having  developed their own unique skill sets  for the sake of contributing to ichigo's  efforts and Urdu someone who once wanted  nothing more than to defeat humiliate  and remove Ichigo from the picture  specifically puts himself into  tremendous danger for the sake of  helping each go in his hour of beat and  following this otter low point with Urdu  shaking looking at ginjou with Orihime  and Chad compromised with Ichigo feeling  utterly alone and betrayed that's when  quite literally my favorite moment in  this series occurs  now to be clear this hasn't been a  series that's particularly tugged on my  heartstrings too much there's been  fleeting moments with orihime's goodbye  during the irankar arc that hit the spot  but truthfully I have not come close to  being too emotional but and I mean this  the feeling of Despair Kubo managed to  craft in this moment that high emotional  stake with the rewriting of history and  compromising everyone we love when  Ichigo turns around to discover Rukia  standing there as if like a guardian  angel someone finally who can offer  genuine help it reminded me of that  scene from end game fondly enough where  everyone comes through the portal at the  end to make the save on Captain America  seeing all of the captains we've  befriended come to the rescue offering  their power to Ichigo to win the day is  magnificently cathartic particularly  because we're doing it all for the  reasons ginjou and tsukushima are trying  to override because he go has genuinely  made an impact not only in this world  not only in his friend's world as  orihime's love for him is evident even  through her brainwashing but also in the  world of the Soul Society making this  very scene on top of all of that  narratively and emotionally earned in my  book well well well  how the turntables  no longer outnumbered each Captain takes  a battle that suits their own character  and due to us having spent a significant  amount of time with the other characters  we can actually enjoy those fights now  too not just because we know them mind  you but because this Arc hasn't shoved  fighting down my neck over and over and  because of that this section feels a  little more novel as a result  furthermore an example of something I  really appreciated in this story was how  Kubo didn't spend two or three chapters  on each individual fight before showing  a flashback to end it all Instead This  Arc dedicates a single chapter chapter  471 to the flashbacks of all of these  allies of ginjou together and the  delivery of this information in this way  serves these characters tremendously  well as this sort of shared group of  trauma that acts as The Binding which  unites them all it saves time and keeps  the pacing Snappy with each POV given a  unique background to help differentiate  them from each other within the chapter  itself yakiya's fight with tsukushima in  the end was again another affair that  forced an aspect of byakia outside of  his comfort zone creating a situation  where he couldn't rely on his ability to  diligently and dutifully prepare but one  where he had to embrace The Madness of  the moment enjoying something more akin  to what Kim patchy might enjoy funnily  enough forcing tsukushima to challenge  him head on something piakya points out  tsukushima isn't comfortable with so I  think this might be the first time I'm  reading a conclusion to a bleach Arc  where pretty much all of the antagonists  hit their Mark for me well okay except  for that one guy who likes time we  didn't really get to know him but that's  okay because Kubo recognizes that too  and had Kenpachi won't hit KO him in the  beginning which was just hilarious if  this was the Iraq Iraq it would have  taken another five chapters but I  digress with the full bring Arc itself  culminating on a single decision Ichigo  needs to make and it's a decision based  on trust ginjou tries to convince him of  the lies the soul Society have Laden him  with and paints a very dark picture that  contrasts what he thought his  relationship was however and I think  fittingly Ichigo irrespective of this  information reveal as he has suspected  it prior and that he still trusts them  because of course he would they came in  his hour of need they let him settle  this on his own terms and as we observed  ourse